# No mirrored enum catalogs

If a change would **hard-code Kotlin/backend enum names** (or closed catalog membership) in **Python** or the **frontend** — stop and **ask** whether that is really wanted.

Prefer: the server exposes metadata (e.g. `GET /api/ai/training/scenarios` with family / flags), and clients cache or consume that list.

Exceptions only when the user explicitly accepts a mirror (or the value is a harness *policy* knob, not catalog membership).

See [`ai/OWNERSHIP.md`](../../ai/OWNERSHIP.md).
